✅ 30-second answer (memorize)

“ServletInitializer is used when we deploy Spring Boot as a WAR on an external server.
That server does not run main(), so SpringBootServletInitializer hooks into the servlet container startup and launches the Spring Boot application.
For normal JAR + embedded Tomcat we don’t need it.”
